    page('V6 engine CAD assembly','SolidWorks assembly practice with original engine renders.','project_v6.html','''<a class="breadcrumb" href="index.html#library">← Project library</a><p class="eyebrow">Mechanical design / CAD practice</p><h1>V6 engine CAD assembly.</h1><p class="lead">A SolidWorks practice assembly exploring component relationships, model organization, clearances, and kinematics.</p><div class="note">CAD practice project. The available artifacts are assembly renders; manufacturing, combustion performance, and physical engine testing are not documented.</div><section class="lab-panel"><h2>Assembly reasoning</h2><p>The original project focused on understanding a complex multi-part assembly and the interaction of its components. Clearance and kinematic relationships are useful design checks, but rendered geometry alone cannot establish tolerance, strength, or operating performance.</p><p><strong>Next evidence:</strong> add an assembly tree, a section view through the cranktrain, and a documented interference or motion study.</p></section><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="engine2.jpeg" alt="Original SolidWorks V6 engine assembly render, first view" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Original project render · assembly view.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="engine1.jpeg" alt="Original SolidWorks V6 engine assembly render, second view" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Original project render · alternate view.</figcaption></figure></div>''')
    page('Mars mission requirements review','Original 77-page Team 13 L’SPACE concept review.','srr_viewer_fixed.html','''<a class="breadcrumb" href="projects/lspace.html">← Mars rover case study</a><p class="eyebrow">NASA L’SPACE / Team 13</p><h1>Mission requirements review.</h1><p class="lead">The original 77-page team document includes requirements, subsystem architecture, trade studies, interface control, and risk analysis. This is a concept-stage review.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="Team%2013%20SRR.pdf" download>Download review PDF ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="Team%2013%20SRR.pdf">Open PDF ↗</a></div><div class="lab-panel"><iframe title="Team 13 Mars mission requirements review PDF" src="Team%2013%20SRR.pdf"></iframe><p>If the embedded viewer is unavailable on your device, use the PDF links above.</p></div>''')
    body='''<a class="breadcrumb" href="projects/thermofluids.html">← Thermofluids case study</a><p class="eyebrow">Interactive engineering model</p><h1>Ideal Brayton cycle.</h1><p class="lead">Explore how pressure ratio and specific heat ratio affect ideal thermal efficiency. This demonstration uses constant specific heats, isentropic compression/expansion, and no pressure losses.</p><div class="lab-panel"><form id="cycle-form" novalidate><div class="inputs"><label for="pr">Pressure ratio P₂/P₁<input id="pr" type="number" value="8" min="1.01" step="0.1" required></label><label for="gamma">Specific heat ratio γ<input id="gamma" type="number" value="1.4" min="1.01" max="1.67" step="0.01" required></label><label for="T1">Inlet temperature (K)<input id="T1" type="number" value="300" min="1" step="1" required></label></div><button class="button" style="margin-top:24px" type="submit">Calculate cycle →</button></form><p id="result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><canvas id="chart" width="900" height="420" role="img" aria-label="Temperature at four cycle states; numerical temperatures are listed above">State temperatures are listed in the calculation result above.</canvas><p class="evidence">The horizontal axis is cycle state, not entropy. Heat addition uses the retained illustration parameter T₃ = 2.5 T₂; it is not measured turbine data.</p></div><section class="lab-panel"><h2>Model equations</h2><p>T₂ = T₁ rₚ<sup>(γ−1)/γ</sup> &nbsp; · &nbsp; T₃ = 2.5 T₂ &nbsp; · &nbsp; T₄ = T₃ / rₚ<sup>(γ−1)/γ</sup></p><p>η = 1 − 1 / rₚ<sup>(γ−1)/γ</sup></p><details><summary>Inspect the JavaScript implementation</summary><pre id="source-code">'''+E((ROOT/'thermo.js').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))+'''</pre></details><p><a href="thermo.js">Open the source file</a></p></section><script src="thermo.js"></script>'''
    page('Ideal Brayton cycle visualizer','Interactive ideal Brayton efficiency and state-temperature model.','thermo_demo_full.html',body)
